## Docker

{% if choices.docker == "full" -%}
Mode: **everything in Docker**. `docker-compose.yml` has two services:

- `dev` (profile `dev`, stage `dev` of `Dockerfile`, image `rust:1.98-slim-trixie` with `rustfmt` and `clippy`): mounts the project folder at `/app`, keeps `target/` and the crate cache (`CARGO_HOME=/home/dev/.cargo`) in the named volumes `target` and `cargo`, runs as user `dev` (uid 1000) with `init: true`. `docker compose up dev` runs `scripts/dev.sh`; `docker compose run --rm dev <command>` runs anything else. After changing dependencies nothing extra is needed: cargo downloads them into the volume.
- `app`: the production image (below). `docker compose run --rm --build app <args>` rebuilds it when needed and runs the tool.
{%- else -%}
Mode: **Docker to run the app**. Development, tests and the native macOS binary use Rust on the host; Docker builds and runs a Linux image of the tool.
{%- endif %}

- `Dockerfile`: the `build` stage (`rust:1.98-slim-trixie`) compiles dependencies first with a placeholder `main.rs` (cached until `Cargo.toml`/`Cargo.lock` change), then `cargo build --release --locked`. The runtime image `gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian13:nonroot` contains only `/usr/local/bin/{{ env.APP_SLUG }}`, runs as a non-root user, uses the tool as `ENTRYPOINT` (default arguments: `--help`) and `/work` as the working directory. `.env` is never copied into images.
- `docker-compose.yml` reads `.env`: `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` ({{ project.slug }}) names the stack and the image `{{ project.slug }}:latest`, `APP_NAME` is a build argument (the binary needs it at build time). The `app` service mounts the project folder at `/work`, so relative paths work: `docker compose run --rm app stats README.md`. `RUST_LOG` is passed through from your shell.
- The tool keeps no state, so there is no data volume: it reads and writes files in the folder it runs in.
- Commands: `docker compose build app`, `docker compose run --rm --build app <args>`, `docker compose{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --profile dev{% endif %} down --rmi all{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --volumes{% endif %}` (removes the containers{% if choices.docker == "full" %}, images and the `target`/`cargo` volumes{% else %} and the image{% endif %}).
- The build stage copies only `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `build.rs` and `src/`. When the build needs more files (e.g. `include_str!("../assets/…")`), add `COPY` lines to the build stage and check `.dockerignore`. Update the `rust:` tag in all stages together.
